  <Scene>
    <WorldInfo title="The Closest Reachable Point" info="&quot;X3D Math Lab • Static sampled geometry and authored lesson parameters; not a proof, live controller, or checkpoint.&quot;">
      <MetadataString containerField="metadata" name="mathlab.sample" reference="mathlab.x3d/1" value="&quot;{\&quot;adapter\&quot;:\&quot;mathlab.x3d/1\&quot;,\&quot;axes\&quot;:\&quot;Spatial coordinates: mathematical (x,y,z). Orbit to separate the target, plane and perpendicular residual.\&quot;,\&quot;bounds\&quot;:{\&quot;center\&quot;:[0.0,0.0,0.057125542138681595],\&quot;size\&quot;:[8.8,7.50221579412365,4.795748915722637]},\&quot;configuration_sha256\&quot;:\&quot;a17b6c647ea7539e5d5ee069aa7d31fe3466314f56b46d5e03467d9885bf7da2\&quot;,\&quot;insights\&quot;:[\&quot;The world uses mathematical coordinates (x,y,z) without flattening. Orbit the camera to see the target, plane, and perpendicular residual.\&quot;,\&quot;Columns a₁=(1,0,0) and a₂=(1,ε cos θ,ε sin θ) remain independent because ε≥0.05. Their span is fixed as ε changes, so the projection stays fixed while coordinates can grow.\&quot;,\&quot;The mint point uses a stable geometric QR calculation with orthonormal basis q₁=(1,0,0), q₂=(0,cos θ,sin θ). The normal-equation coefficients are retained only as a comparison.\&quot;,\&quot;A large condition number describes worst-case sensitivity; it does not say every target has a large error. Drawing the projection directly avoids huge opposing coefficient vectors obscuring its geometry.\&quot;],\&quot;lesson\&quot;:\&quot;least_squares\&quot;,\&quot;metrics\&quot;:[{\&quot;id\&quot;:\&quot;residual\&quot;,\&quot;label\&quot;:\&quot;Closest distance ||b−p||\&quot;,\&quot;note\&quot;:\&quot;\&quot;,\&quot;unit\&quot;:\&quot;\&quot;,\&quot;value\&quot;:1.163076821608171},{\&quot;id\&quot;:\&quot;orthogonality\&quot;,\&quot;label\&quot;:\&quot;Max |aⱼ·(b−p)|\&quot;,\&quot;note\&quot;:\&quot;Zero is the analytic optimality condition; this is a floating-point diagnostic.\&quot;,\&quot;unit\&quot;:\&quot;\&quot;,\&quot;value\&quot;:5.551115123125783e-17},{\&quot;id\&quot;:\&quot;coefficient_1\&quot;,\&quot;label\&quot;:\&quot;Coefficient x̂₁\&quot;,\&quot;note\&quot;:\&quot;\&quot;,\&quot;unit\&quot;:\&quot;\&quot;,\&quot;value\&quot;:-2.4557683767741656},{\&quot;id\&quot;:\&quot;coefficient_2\&quot;,\&quot;label\&quot;:\&quot;Coefficient x̂₂\&quot;,\&quot;note\&quot;:\&quot;\&quot;,\&quot;unit\&quot;:\&quot;\&quot;,\&quot;value\&quot;:3.8557683767741655},{\&quot;id\&quot;:\&quot;condition\&quot;,\&quot;label\&quot;:\&quot;2-norm condition number κ₂(A)\&quot;,\&quot;note\&quot;:\&quot;κ₂(AᵀA)=κ₂(A)². The display solves by the known orthonormal basis rather than forming the normal equations.\&quot;,\&quot;unit\&quot;:\&quot;\&quot;,\&quot;value\&quot;:3.932042912437429}],\&quot;parameters\&quot;:{\&quot;bx\&quot;:1.4,\&quot;by\&quot;:1.2,\&quot;bz\&quot;:2.1,\&quot;epsilon\&quot;:0.55,\&quot;tilt\&quot;:0.55},\&quot;sample_schema\&quot;:\&quot;mathlab.sample/1\&quot;,\&quot;sample_sha256\&quot;:\&quot;ae35593f041018c03e9ee1a5690b3302903e73dd816c469db7eb571cebb7a64c\&quot;,\&quot;scope\&quot;:\&quot;Static sampled geometry and authored lesson parameters; not a proof, live controller, or checkpoint.\&quot;,\&quot;title\&quot;:\&quot;The Closest Reachable Point\&quot;,\&quot;view\&quot;:\&quot;spatial\&quot;}&quot;" />
